  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe four debug suites of issue 1716 spent their time in HSM plans at the default optimal load (0.1464 of D). One 2D Adaptive plan on the 30 mm block took about 130 s in debug. The suites now run their adaptive plans at 0.4 of D. The fixture geometry, the asserts and the laws do not change. No file under `crates/*/src` changes.\n\n- `whole_model_pocket`: `adaptive()` uses `LOAD = 0.4`. A new `#[ignore]`d twin, `a_whole_part_adaptive_at_the_default_load_keeps_the_full_tool_radius_off_the_part` (heavy lane, release), keeps the disc law at the default load.\n- `pocket_overhead`, `climb_direction`: `pocket()` uses `optimal_load: 0.4`. Only the `Adaptive` strategy reads it.\n- `adaptive_pinch`: `retyped()` sets `optimal_load = 0.4` for `Adaptive2D` only. `Offset2D` has no load.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1716-lighter-hsm-fixtures.md`.\n\n`#[test]` count: 11 before, 12 after (one new ignored twin). No assert is removed. No golden changes.\n\n## Times (debug, one binary at a time, this Windows machine)\n\n| Binary | Before (triage table) | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `whole_model_pocket` | 125 s | 1.7 s |\n| `pocket_overhead` | 58 s | 9.1 s |\n| `climb_direction` | 38 s | 6.0 s |\n| `adaptive_pinch` | 59 s | 8.2 s |\n\n## What each changed test guards, and the mutation checks\n\nEach mutation was a temporary edit of `src`, built and run, then reverted. It is not in the PR.\n\n| Mutation (temporary) | Law | Result at load 0.4 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `machining2d::chord_clears` returns `true` after the end-point checks | chord law between pieces (#1620) | `adaptive_pinch` fails: \"Adaptive2D turned false: a cut ... 3.828 into the disc\". `whole_model_pocket` 4 of 5 fail. |\n| `pocket_region_on_part` ignores the standing part | region under a closed floor | `pocket_overhead` both tests fail (no refusal under the floor). |\n| `pocket_hsm` plans with `!p.climb` | cut direction of the HSM wall pass (#1555) | `climb_direction` fails: \"Adaptive climb=true: wall pass swept -200\". |\n| `area::around_part` returns the stock outline | whole-part island law (#12, #42) | `whole_model_pocket` all 5 fail (verify 1681 warnings, no refusal, generated path gouges). |\n\nWhy the smaller load still guards the law: the island region, the full-radius disc check, the chord law and the cut direction do not read the ring step. Each mutation above fails the changed test at the new load. The default load stays covered by the new twin and by the release-lane test of `adaptive_pinch`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- The four binaries, in debug: all pass (times above).\n- The new twin, run in debug with `--ignored`: passes in 137 s.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test whole_model_pocket --test pocket_overhead --test climb_direction --test adaptive_pinch -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The new twin in release mode (it ran only in debug).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick` as a whole (the four touched binaries ran one by one).\n- Other OSes.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1716\n",
